      "problem": "Lily bought $8$ small cakes for $$12.$ At what unit price did Lily pay?",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of dollars to cakes is $12:8.$ Expressing this as a fraction, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{8}\n$$\n\nWe can reduce this fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷4}{8÷4}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the unit price Lily paid is $\\frac{3}{2}$ of a dollar per cake.",
